HBO's new miniseries Chernobyl recounts  the 1986 nuclear disaster in Ukraine  it's a dramatization so while many  events depicted in the show are based in  reality it had a few discrepancies with  historical accounts here are 12 of them  see that thick pillar of black smoke  that's coming out of the power plant it  makes for an ominous shot but in reality  it was more likely thin trails of white  vapor that were escaping from the  reactor in Episode one Game of Thrones  fans might have recognized donald Sumter  the actor who played maester Luwin it  turns out that his character in  Chernobyl an elderly Bolshevik by the  name of Zarkov is fictional his speech  urging officials not to raise alarm  about the accident that's also a  fabrication no one leaves and cut the  phone lines contain the spread of  misinformation that doesn't mean there  wasn't some effort to contain the spread  of information in the immediate  aftermath of the meltdown but we don't  know if what Zarkov says here accurately  reflects the government's rationale at  this point in time Chernobyl is the  biggest nuclear accident to date but  according to Jan haverkamp a senior  nuclear energy expert at Greenpeace  Lagasse's comparison of Chernobyl to  Hiroshima doesn't quite make sense the  fire were watching with our own eyes is  giving off any twice the radiation  released by the bomb in Hiroshima the  bomb dropped on Hiroshima was so  devastating because of the number of  people that suffered direct exposure to  radiation at Chernobyl on the other hand  radioactive material enters atmosphere  and disperses so it's health effects  were more indirect and long-term  in Episode two a helicopter crashes as  it flies over the open reactor there was  a helicopter crash in the wake of  Chernobyl but the show moved this event  up chronologically the crash actually  took place in October of that year  months after they were done fighting the  fire of the fictional characters in the  show the most central is Ilana home yuk  the scientists from the Belarusian  Institute for nuclear energy home yuk  travels to Chernobyl uninvited  interrogate the plant supervisors in  their hospital rooms and soon enough  even finds herself in the presence of  general secretary Gorbachev if that  storyline seems unrealistic for one  person it's because home yuk was  imagined as a composite character to  represent the many scientists who led  the cleanup effort her gender is  definitely realistic as the USSR had an  impressive record of training women for  stem roles in Episode two homie ik warns  the council that a second explosion  could occur ejecting even more  radioactive material from the core at a  force of up to four megatons  according to Haverkamp that estimate is  probably an exaggeration the rest of her  description doesn't quite hold up either  unlikely be fatal to the entire  population of Kiev as well as a portion  of Minsk and will impact all of Soviet  Ukraine Latvia Lithuania Belarus eeeh as  well as Poland Czechoslovakia Hungary  Romania and most of his journey the  assertion that all of Europe would be  affected involves a lot of hypotheticals  as Haverkamp says that situation might  play out if all of the melt and khorium  hit ground water but when khorium starts  melting it does so in a very uneven way  so if the second explosion had actually  occurred it'd be pretty difficult to  predict the fallout  as part of the effort to prevent the  steam explosion that homi accord about  three patriotic volunteers dive into  radioactive water to open the tank  valves the show takes a few liberties  here according to one of the divers  Alexei Annan enco they didn't all  volunteer for the job Annan nkow was an  engineer at the plant who simply  happened to be on duty that day when his  supervisor assigned him to the mission  he was told he could refuse the  assignment but he was the only person on  the shift who knew the location of the  valves leaving him with effectively no  choice but to join the team of divers in  one of the series more comical moments  the miners digging the tunnel underneath  unit 3 strip naked took hope with the  heat it's possible that a few of the  miners actually did this but even the  show's writer and creator Craig Mazin  said that there were some varying  accounts of how much clothing got taken  off one of the sources at Mazin  consulted was midnight in Chernobyl a  book based on real accounts of the  accident compiled by journalist Adam  Higginbotham in an interview with  inverse Higginbotham said the show  exaggerated the denial and delayed  response of the Soviet government his  book describes how the investigation  into Chernobyl began almost immediately  on several fronts within 36 hours of the  explosion reactor specialists traveled  to Chernobyl from Moscow and were able  to promptly identify the most likely  cause of the accident  therefore as Higginbotham said there was  no need for a crusading whistleblower to  uncover the causes but raising awareness  about the problems that led to Chernobyl  did take Soviet scientists several years  of hard work and research sadly the  friendship we see developed between  Boris cher bina chairman of the  Chernobyl Commission and Valery legassik  the chief scientific investigator was  largely an imagined one the duo scenes  together show their growing bond but  there's no evidence that any of these  scenes actually happened look off was  also not quite the martyr figure that  Jared Harris  pics raising his voice to Gorbachev an  openly challenging the head of the KGB  we have no reason to think that the  trial of Dyatlov and the other two plant  managers involved any of the theatrics  seen in the finale when legassik  denounces his government in front of a  room of officials the gossip did die by  suicide two years after the explosion  and he did dictate a final letter  reflecting on the liquidation effort he  spearheaded but in this message he  didn't ask what is the costs of lies the  show's tagline nor did he contemplate  any abstract questions about the meaning  of truth the real danger is that if we  hear enough lies then we no longer  recognize the truth at all the goshawk  did have concrete grievances about the  handling of chernobyl which he outlined  in great detail in his message did we  miss anything let us know in the  comments  you
 

